{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Jig1F1MhaAWCwbpsMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Your answers would change what the letter asks for and how it handles the weak spot:\n\n1. **Is there a senior paralegal opening, or would this create a new role?** If the group has no senior paralegal now, the letter has to explain why the group needs one, not just why you deserve it. If the role exists or is opening up, the letter can go straight to your fit for it.\n2. **Does the managing partner already know about the March deadline error?** If they do, the letter should bring it up first and show the second-person check as the fix. If they don't, we can decide together whether to include it. I'd lean toward including it, because hearing about it from someone else later would hurt more.\n3. **Would any of the 4 lawyers you support back the request?** If so, can I name them, or say that you've talked with them?\n4. **What did you do on the 2 trial cases?** For example, trial binders, exhibits, managing witnesses, or being at counsel table. One concrete detail would do more than the case count alone.\n5. **What's the timing, and what do you want to happen next?** Is this tied to annual reviews or a budget cycle? Are you asking for a meeting, or for a decision by a certain date? And is it going as an email or as a formal letter?\n\nIf you don't know some of these, just say so and I'll write it without them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":9548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18525811-6564-415f-b